WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.960
Gemma’s influence over club matters?&nbsp;
The shifting narrative of John Teller’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:10.000
death? The Galindo cartel deal? Keep&nbsp;
watching as we get into some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.400
most questionable things from "Sons&nbsp;
of Anarchy" that we just let slide.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.120
We're not sure any of the questionable&nbsp;
things we've come up with really rival&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:24.320
the seemingly boundless loyalty that&nbsp;
Harry "Opie" Winston shows SAMCRO.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:30.400
He does five years in Chino prison after former&nbsp;
member Kyle Hobart ditches him and tries to stay&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:36.160
on the straight and narrow upon his release in&nbsp;
order to keep his wife Donna happy. Nonetheless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:41.760
it's clear Opie misses the brotherhood he enjoyed&nbsp;
as a member of the club — as evidenced by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:47.200
way he is eventually drawn back in by best&nbsp;
friend Jax Teller to make some extra money.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:53.840
Unfortunately, repeated attempts by ATF Agent&nbsp;
June Stahl to get Opie to turn on the club&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:58.240
result in president Clay Morrow&nbsp;
believing Opie truly is a rat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:06.480
so Clay orders Alexander "Tig" Trager to kill him.&nbsp;
As fans know, Tig mistakenly kills Donna instead.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:11.840
Opie, of course, is at first unaware his own&nbsp;
club is responsible for his wife's death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:18.000
Eventually, Tig confesses out of guilt, at&nbsp;
which point Opie gives him a savage beating.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.000
He still stays with the club nonetheless, seeing&nbsp;
Stahl as the real villain; it doesn't hurt that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Clay spares his father, Piney, after the&nbsp;
elder Winston fires a gun at him twice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.960
But Clay has only hit pause on eliminating members&nbsp;
of Opie's family: he kills Piney in Season 4 over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:42.560
letters Jax's father wrote, which indicate his&nbsp;
seeming awareness that Clay and Jax's mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:49.440
Gemma Teller, are going to kill him. Opie shoots&nbsp;
Clay twice, but is still able to operate alongside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:55.440
him and Tig up until he finally gives his&nbsp;
own life for the club in prison in Season 5.

00:01:57.276 --> 00:02:03.680
Jax Teller is ostensibly all about family. First,&nbsp;
his devotion to his brothers in SAMCRO is rivaled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:10.560
only by Opie's. Jax fights to maintain custody of&nbsp;
his son Abel from his drug-addicted ex-wife Wendy.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.400
"Please don't hate me."

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.120
"You need to get help, Wendy."

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:18.400
"I know, I know, I promise this time, I promise."

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:26.080
He drags the entire SAMCRO crew to Ireland in&nbsp;
Season 3 to track Abel down after he's kidnapped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:33.760
by True IRA bad guy Cameron Hayes. Jax actually&nbsp;
considers leaving SAMCRO to get his wife Tara and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:40.720
their two sons away from the outlaw life. And, of&nbsp;
course, he sacrifices himself in the series finale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:45.760
so that SAMCRO can remain operational,&nbsp;
given the mayhem vote against him.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:52.240
But in his travels to the old sod, Jax learns&nbsp;
he has a half-sister, Trinity — a product of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:58.640
an affair between his father John Teller and&nbsp;
Maureen Ashby — a fact of which he learns just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:04.160
in the knick of time before the two got too cozy&nbsp;
with each other. Obviously they're both pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:09.600
embarrassed to have almost hooked up with a blood&nbsp;
relative and maybe that awkwardness is the reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:15.920
we never hear from Trinity and Maureen again;&nbsp;
despite Jax being more focused on family than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:22.720
the entire "Fast and Furious" saga, his long-lost&nbsp;
sibling remains a Season 3 ghost and doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:28.320
surface again for the remaining four seasons&nbsp;
of "Sons of Anarchy." The awkwardness of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:33.840
introduction notwithstanding, it doesn't make&nbsp;
sense that we never hear from the Ashbys again.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:39.680
We're thinking maybe Jax Teller needs a&nbsp;
dictionary; could someone turn him to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:45.680
page that defines the word "legitimate"? We're&nbsp;
all about him taking SAMCRO away from drugs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:51.600
guns and the respective precarious relationships&nbsp;
with cartels and the Irish Republican Army that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:58.480
those dealings represent. But getting into the&nbsp;
"companion" business is no less illegal. Look,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:04.480
we get that Nero Padilla is a charming guy, and&nbsp;
if we had to pick a fictional character of shady&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:09.920
repute with whom our outlaw mother would hook up,&nbsp;
it would be him. We could debate the respective&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:15.440
moralities of the Sons being smugglers against&nbsp;
working in the sex trade, but at the end of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:21.200
day, there's simply no getting around the simple&nbsp;
fact that they're both against the law. Trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:27.280
to take the club legit by leaving drugs and guns&nbsp;
in favor of escorts is like trying to lose weight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:33.600
by simply switching from full-calorie Coke to&nbsp;
full-calorie Pepsi — it's just not going to work.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:39.040
Of course, all of that being said, it's also true&nbsp;
that Jax's first attempt to get the club to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:45.520
legit would have worked if Clay hadn't torpedoed&nbsp;
it. Putting SAMCRO in the adult film business in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:52.000
Season 2 with Luann Delaney's film studio Cara&nbsp;
Cara was at least a legitimate business venture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:58.720
operating within the law. Of course, Cara Cara&nbsp;
also provided a source of relationship drama&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:05.280
between Jax and future wife Tara Knowles, but&nbsp;
it's also where Opie met his second wife, Lyla.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:11.280
Juan Carlos "Juice" Ortiz manages&nbsp;
a lot of the non-muscle tasks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:16.640
SAMCRO faces over the course of the "Sons&nbsp;
of Anarchy" timeline. He's technologically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:22.080
proficient and serves the role of an MC's&nbsp;
version of a hacker and tech support,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:26.720
but he's also prone to making his share&nbsp;
of stupid decisions — perhaps the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:32.400
notable of which is turning against the club&nbsp;
when Sheriff Eli Roosevelt blackmails him.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:38.240
Back in the day, when the Sons of Anarchy&nbsp;
Motorcycle Club was first formed, the legendary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:44.320
First 9 — the founding members of the Redwood&nbsp;
Original chapter — wrote their bylaws with some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:50.480
rules that would not age well. Among them was the&nbsp;
provision that prohibited Black men as members.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:55.840
Sheriff Roosevelt blackmails Juice on&nbsp;
behalf of Season 4's primary antagonist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.840 --> 00:06:01.600
Lincoln Potter, knowing that Juice's father is&nbsp;
Black, threatening to reveal his heritage to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:07.200
club if he doesn't turn snitch. Fearing being&nbsp;
kicked out of the club, Juice does Potter's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:13.280
bidding and steals a brick of cocaine — which will&nbsp;
provide proof that SAMCRO is mixed up with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:20.160
Galindo Cartel — and even kills Eric Miles when&nbsp;
he's caught in the act trying to return the drugs.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:22.240
"Doesn't make sense. Miles?"

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:28.320
The inanity we ignore is that Juice would&nbsp;
rather risk getting caught out as a rat — for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:33.280
which he'd almost certainly be killed — than&nbsp;
potentially get kicked out of the club over an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:37.760
outdated rule that it's possible no one&nbsp;
in the modern club would even care about.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:44.240
Speaking of the outdated rules written by the&nbsp;
founding members of the Sons of Anarchy MC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:49.680
in addition to people of color, women were&nbsp;
also prohibited from being members of the club.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:54.000
So, while it's true that Gemma and Tara&nbsp;
are not patched members of the club,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:58.880
it's unlikely that any woman would be able&nbsp;
to exert as much influence on its comings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:05.360
and goings as the two of them do — and Gemma more&nbsp;
than anyone. Biker culture has traditionally been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:10.880
patriarchal in nature, and the club that's&nbsp;
presented on "Sons of Anarchy" is no different.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:15.040
Don't take our word for it; people have&nbsp;
written scholarly articles about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:19.520
persistence of patriarchy in the&nbsp;
world of motorcycle aficionados.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:25.120
In her thesis "Making Sense Of Motorcycle&nbsp;
Brotherhood: Women, Branding, And Construction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:30.960
Of Self," Kimberly Michelle Maas notes that the&nbsp;
number of women riders has risen over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:38.960
but is still down around 25% of the total biker&nbsp;
population, with 75% being men. She concludes:

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:41.680
"No matter the experience used to define&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:47.120
or support patriarchy in motorcycles the&nbsp;
data shows that it still does exist."

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:51.520
Quora user George Paczolt&nbsp;
addressed Gemma's role in the club,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:56.320
after laying out an impressive list&nbsp;
of his MC credentials. He wrote:

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:00.240
"Gemma's position in the club ain't&nbsp;
gonna happen — ever. She'd have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:05.120
taken out back and 'corrected' halfway&nbsp;
thru the first episode in the real world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:09.920
Women do not have any decision making&nbsp;
positions in a real M/C. Period."

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:16.000
The mystery and uncertainty behind John&nbsp;
Teller's death plays a crucial role in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:21.520
early development of "Sons of Anarchy," and his&nbsp;
figurative ghost — the narrative set forth in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:27.760
his manuscript "The Life and Death of Sam Crow:&nbsp;
How the Sons of Anarchy Lost Their Way" — also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:34.320
helps set up conflict between Jax and Clay. JT&nbsp;
makes it clear he feels the club's decision to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:41.360
get into guns with the True IRA was a catalyst&nbsp;
for SAMCRO's seeming downfall and tries more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:47.360
once to get the club out of guns and into more&nbsp;
legitimate pursuits — sound familiar? Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:52.960
Jax's father died shortly after completing&nbsp;
this manuscript, so the subtext reads that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.960 --> 00:09:00.080
his idea wasn't popular with a certain party who&nbsp;
very much wants SAMCRO to continue running guns.

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:06.560
Initially, we're told JT died in an accident, but&nbsp;
the circumstances change more than once. Gemma&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:13.920
suggests that, following the death of their second&nbsp;
son, Thomas, JT may have taken his own life. JT's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:20.400
letters to Maureen Ashby indicate he feels like&nbsp;
Clay and Gemma are plotting to kill him. We also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:27.120
find out that Wayne Unser helped cover up the fact&nbsp;
that his bike was sabotaged, so it was murder. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:34.560
then it was neither an accident nor murder because&nbsp;
JT's confidant Jury White insists JT would know if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:40.320
his bike had been tampered with, suggesting he&nbsp;
purposely crashed his bike into the semi in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:47.200
effort to save the club and keep SAMCRO together.&nbsp;
Given how Jax met his own end, we assume the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:52.960
recent version of JT's death is what he chose to&nbsp;
believe, but the shifting narrative on the matter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:58.960
of John Teller's death was definitely a source&nbsp;
of frustration for many "Sons of Anarchy" fans.

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:05.040
Robert "Bobby Elvis" Munson is a nuanced&nbsp;
and important character among the "Sons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:11.600
of Anarchy" cast. He serves as both a surrogate&nbsp;
father figure and vital sounding board for Jax,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:17.520
talking the volatile young man down with a skilled&nbsp;
and steady hand on more than one occasion. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:23.680
many situations that called for a voice of reason,&nbsp;
Bobby plays that role, knowing the tension between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:30.400
Clay and Jax is bad for the club as a whole. He&nbsp;
also initially serves as vice president of SAMCRO&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:36.560
when Jax takes the president's patch. Before&nbsp;
that, Bobby Elvis serves as club treasurer, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:42.880
it's in this capacity that the character is seen&nbsp;
acting outside his normal operating principles.

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:48.800
In Season 2, when reviewing the finances of&nbsp;
the club's joint venture with Luann Delaney,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:56.080
the Cara Cara adult film studio, Bobby realizes&nbsp;
Luann is skimming and thus defrauding SAMCRO&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.080 --> 00:11:00.880
of money. Based on the moral compass he&nbsp;
presents throughout the rest of the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:06.000
we'd expect Bobby to turn Luann in to&nbsp;
face the consequences of her actions.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:10.560
"By my calculations, you've been&nbsp;
cutting us light for six years."

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:17.520
Instead, he gives into her advances and chooses&nbsp;
not to disclose her theft. It's a decision that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:22.640
doesn't make sense, given Bobby's tendency&nbsp;
to do what's best for the club. Further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:28.320
Luann is Otto Delaney's old lady. Despite the&nbsp;
fact that the prison clause — we're still not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:32.400
sure if that's actually a thing in&nbsp;
real life MC culture, but we hope&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:38.240
not — allows other members to have relations&nbsp;
with an old lady while her man is in prison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:43.040
it's just wrong on so many levels and not&nbsp;
really in keeping with the character as a whole.

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:51.120
Season 4 has a 100% critics score on Rotten&nbsp;
Tomatoes — a peculiar score considering there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:56.480
a major issue with the finale. Assistant&nbsp;
U.S. Attorney Lincoln Potter rolls into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.480 --> 00:12:02.400
town as members of SAMCRO are released&nbsp;
from prison and recruits Eli Roosevelt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:09.200
the new top dog at the San Joaquin County Sheriff&nbsp;
Department, to be a part of his multi-agency task&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:16.560
force to bring down SAMCRO, the True IRA, and&nbsp;
Russian organized crime all in one fell swoop.

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:21.200
Potter sows dissension in the ranks&nbsp;
by forcing Juice to betray his club&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:27.680
in order to remain a member when he and Roosevelt&nbsp;
convince the wayward Juan Carlos to steal a brick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:35.840
of cocaine SAMCRO got from the Galindo Cartel&nbsp;
— represented by Romero "Romeo" Parada and Luis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:42.960
Torres Potter is an antagonist who's ambitious&nbsp;
and cunning to boot. In fact, he's so good that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:49.520
looks like he's got all his ducks in a row and is&nbsp;
about to clear the board with a massive RICO case.

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:52.960
Then the cartel shows up to make that all go away.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:59.680
See, Parada and Torres are actually members&nbsp;
of the CIA working on a black-book operation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:04.800
and the American government is backing the&nbsp;
Galindo cartel in the hopes of putting other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:09.760
cartels out of business and eliminating&nbsp;
the violence between the warring factions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:16.080
amid other political reasons. It doesn't matter&nbsp;
that Potter succeeded where others had failed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:22.480
because this deus ex machina ending essentially&nbsp;
undid the entire season's worth of drama.

